                  Migration Vs Without Migration
===========================================================================

The "Dual-Work" Trap (Manually Syncing Code & DB):
Every time you add, change, or delete a property in your C# models, you have to manually open a database tool (like MySQL Workbench) and write raw SQL commands to match it.

With Migrations: You change C# $\rightarrow$ Run command $\rightarrow$ Database updates automatically.
Without Migrations: You change C# $\rightarrow$ You manually write ALTER TABLE Users ADD Column Phone VARCHAR(20); in MySQL. If you make a typo in the database column name, your app crashes.




================================================= 
   DEVELOPMENT vs PRODUCTION 
================================================

Think of your software development cycle in two distinct phases: 
Construction (Development) and Operation (Production).

---

### Phase 1: Construction (Building the House)

This is where `dotnet-ef` and `EFCore.Design` work. They act as the architect and blueprint machines.

 They only run on your laptop/development machine.
 Their sole job is to look at your C# classes and write out the blueprint files (the `Migrations` folder in your code).
 Once the blueprints are generated, their job is completely finished.

---

### Phase 2: Operation (Living in the House)

When you publish your API or Web App and ship it to a server (like AWS, Azure, or a Linux VPS), you do not ship `dotnet-ef` or `EFCore.Design`. They are left behind.

 The live running application doesn't need to generate blueprints anymore; it just needs to read and write data.
 The only thing running on the server is your App Code and the Pomelo.MySql Provider (the connection pipe to the database).

---

### Summary Checklist

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Package / Tool                           | Needed on your Laptop (Dev)?        | Needed on the Live Server (Prod)? |
| ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| `dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef` | YES (To type commands)              | NO                                |
| `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design`   | YES (To generate C# code files)     | NO                                |
| `Pomelo.EntityFrameworkCore.MySql`       | YES (To connect locally)            | YES (To connect live)             |
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------








